1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,266
Veridelta compares two datasets on their primary keys.

2
00:00:04,266 --> 00:00:08,367
It reports every row that differs, under rules you declare.

3
00:00:08,367 --> 00:00:13,425
Here are 40 accounts, exported before and after a rewrite.

4
00:00:13,425 --> 00:00:16,600
Did the rewrite keep the data the same?

5
00:00:16,600 --> 00:00:21,514
One command compares them on the account ID, with no configuration file.

6
00:00:21,514 --> 00:00:24,796
39 rows changed, and 1 row is gone.

7
00:00:24,796 --> 00:00:28,533
The exit code is 1, so a CI job would fail.

8
00:00:28,533 --> 00:00:33,207
This file names the two exports and the key, with no rules yet.

9
00:00:33,207 --> 00:00:37,665
veridelta suggest tries each kind of rule on the columns that differ.

10
00:00:37,665 --> 00:00:43,203
It proposes a rule for letter case, rounding, and missing notes, each with its evidence.

11
00:00:43,203 --> 00:00:47,267
No model is called. Each rule is one you could write by hand.

12
00:00:47,267 --> 00:00:51,437
The status codes changed too, from words to letters.

13
00:00:51,437 --> 00:00:56,767
crosswalk lines up the values and proposes a map, with how many rows agree.

14
00:00:56,767 --> 00:01:00,313
The configuration now declares all four rules.

15
00:01:00,313 --> 00:01:03,138
Two rows still differ.

16
00:01:03,138 --> 00:01:06,400
Nothing is forgiven unless a rule says so.

17
00:01:06,400 --> 00:01:11,914
Account 40 was removed on purpose, so a baseline file accepts that change.

18
00:01:11,914 --> 00:01:15,520
The run accepts it, and still fails on the other row.

19
00:01:15,520 --> 00:01:19,333
So CI holds the rewrite until that row is fixed.

20
00:01:19,333 --> 00:01:23,311
The HTML report shows that row side by side.

21
00:01:23,311 --> 00:01:28,600
Account 17 moved from south to east. That is the real defect.

22
00:01:28,600 --> 00:01:33,010
Veridelta is early, at version 0.33.

23
00:01:33,010 --> 00:01:36,964
It is tested on generated data, with drift seeded on purpose.

24
00:01:36,964 --> 00:01:41,230
It has not yet been run by other users, or in a live cloud warehouse.

25
00:01:41,230 --> 00:01:43,067
Feedback is welcome.

26
00:01:43,067 --> 00:01:50,133
Try it with pip install veridelta.
